Subject: [PATCH 03090/11362] [outer-loop] unblock .417 PHASE 0 cascade: write
 the missing archive/activate deliverable

The .417 planner referenced python/carnot/experiment_4510_archive_416_activate_417.py
(never created) for the PHASE 0 transition task, but the conductor had ALREADY
performed the archive+activate itself (commit 620016e76; .416 recorded in
research-complete.yaml, research-roadmap.yaml is now .417). So the codex agent
found nothing to diff and the task FAILed 3 consecutive times with 'No file
changes produced' -- a cascade blocking the conductor from reaching PHASE A1
(the frame-change prune predictor, the actual sprint score-lever).

Fix: write the honest close-state deliverable the task was meant to produce
(inference_substrate=aggregation_from_upstream_artifacts; status=success). This
makes _deliverable_exists() short-circuit PHASE 0 to OK so the conductor
advances. Numbers imported from exp4509 capstone (held-out 0.143, variant 0.28,
all 3 score-levers null, lazy value-eval 232x B2) + arc_solve_registry header
(47 levels / 24 games / 1 provisional). adversarial_verify: 0 flagged. No
compute fabricated -- the archive/activate was genuinely done by the conductor.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
